# Document Structure Guidelines

## Section Numbering

- Part I, II, III... for major divisions
- XX_ prefix for files (01_, 02_, etc.)
- X.Y for theorems/derivations within sections
- Consistent cross-references

## Standard Section Template

```markdown
# [Number]. [Title]

## Overview

[1-2 paragraph summary of what this section establishes]

### Key Results

- **[THEOREM/DERIVATION X.Y]**: [one-line summary]
- **[THEOREM/DERIVATION X.Z]**: [one-line summary]

### Prerequisites

This section requires:
- [Section N]: [what concepts]
- [Appendix X]: [what details]

---

## X.1 [First Subsection]

[Content]

---

## X.2 [Second Subsection]

[Content]

---

## Summary

| Result | Type | Status |
|--------|------|--------|
| [name] | THEOREM | Proven |
| [name] | DERIVATION | Complete |
| [name] | CONJECTURE | Open |

## References

- [Internal]: Section Y, Appendix Z
- [External]: [citations]
```

## Part Structure

### Part I: Mathematics (Sections 01-05)
- Pure math, no physics interpretation
- All claims are THEOREMS
- Establishes the geometric foundation

### Part II: Postulates (Sections 06-08)
- The axioms of the theory
- Clearly separated from derivations
- Minimal set of assumptions

### Part III-VI: Derived Physics (Sections 09-26)
- Everything follows from Parts I + II
- Claims are DERIVATIONS or PREDICTIONS
- Physical interpretations included

### Part VII-VIII: Dynamics (Sections 27-33)
- Microscopic theory
- Emergent phenomena
- Some CONJECTURES allowed

### Part IX: Assessment (Sections 34-38)
- Honest evaluation
- Comparison with alternatives
- Open problems

## Cross-Reference Format

```markdown
See [THEOREM 3.2] for the proof.
As established in [POSTULATE 2.1]...
From [DERIVATION 5.3], we have...
Details in [Appendix E.3].
```

## Figure/Table Conventions

- Figures: Figure X.Y (section.number)
- Tables: Table X.Y
- Equations: (X.Y) when numbered
- Code listings: Listing X.Y

## Status Tracking

Each section should end with status:

```markdown
## Section Status

| Claim | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| THEOREM 3.1 | ✅ Proven | Computational verification in D.1 |
| THEOREM 3.2 | ✅ Proven | |
| DERIVATION 3.3 | 🟡 Partial | Step 2 needs work |
| CONJECTURE 3.4 | ⬜ Open | |

**Overall**: [Complete / In Progress / Stub]
```
